From ad61cb30aac8f7f8880fe53da4355535f6edeeaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:37:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a filter's finish code after the reply began asks
 the group's next member (#5075)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A vendor that answers with a canned refusal line as the content and has
its finish_reason "content_filter" follow (#5075: CodeArts's
deepseek-v4.1-flash, 10/10 on the same body, 47 tokens out, the line
byte-identical) was a try that stood as a success: the line had gone out
as content, so the scan's refusal paths were past, only refusedAfter was
marked, the group's next member was never asked, and a client that reads
finish reasons — Pi's and DeepSeek Harness's mapStopReason, Claude Code —
failed the whole turn on it. Another member of the same group answered
620 tokens.

refusalAfter now hands the try over (handOffAfter) when the refusal is
the vendor's own finish code (eventRefusal), the reply is passing, a
candidate stands behind it reading Chat chunks, and no call of the reply
has gone by: what of the write went by before the code goes out with the
reply, the code, its usage and [DONE] do not, and the next member's
chunks follow in the same stream, as a refusal after reasoning is
(handOver). The member isn't set aside: the request was refused, not the
account (#248). A refusal still held goes through the scan's own paths
(flow, handOver) as before; an error event mid-reply stays as it came
(#733); an Anthropic or Responses client's stream is numbered and what
of it has gone by is untracked, so its refusal keeps going as it came.

TestRefusalAfterThinkingAndTextStays becomes
TestRefusalAfterThinkingAndTextFailsOver: a Chat client is handed over
now, where it ended on the vendor's finish code before.

Fixes #5075

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
